{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicy", "label": "snapshotPolicy() -> (seqNr, state, event) => boolean", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaultet auf () => false - das Framework snapshottet nie automatisch. Snapshot-bei-jedem-Event verdoppelt oder verdreifacht die Schreibkosten; wer das will, will wahrscheinlich DurableStateActor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_everynevents", "label": "everyNEvents(N)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "everyNEvents(100) ist ein vernuenftiger Startpunkt; die Recovery-Latenz in Produktion messen, bevor man aendert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore_catalog", "label": "Eingebaute Snapshot Stores", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Journal und Snapshot Store sind unabhaengig und mischbar - z. B. Cassandra-Journal plus Object-Storage-Snapshot-Store."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_recovery_flow_with_snapshots", "label": "Recovery-Flow mit Snapshots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Snapshot ist nur der Punkt, wo das Replay startet; alles danach ist Event-Replay wie ueblich, und onEvent bleibt rein."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_retention_best_effort_write_is_not", "label": "Aufbewahrung ist Best-Effort, der Schreibvorgang nicht", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein fehlgeschlagener Schreibvorgang heisst, dass der Snapshot nicht existiert - ein erneuter Versuch ist richtig, deshalb schlaegt save fehl. Ein fehlgeschlagenes Aufraeumen heisst, dass eine Zeile zu viel existiert - harmlos, loadLatest sieht sie nicht. Das Zweite wie das Erste zu melden wuerde einen Aufrufer einen bereits erfolgreichen Schreibvorgang wiederholen lassen, und ein Actor, der Snapshot-Fehler als fatal behandelt, wuerde an einem Aufraeumfehler sterben."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotadapter", "label": "SnapshotAdapter (State-Schema-Evolution)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Alternative zum Loeschen alter Snapshots: mit gesetztem Adapter werden Snapshots in einem { _v, _t, _e }-Envelope persistiert und beim Laden migriert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_adapter_pairing_rule", "label": "Snapshot-Adapter muessen zum Event-Adapter passen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Haben Events einen Adapter, Snapshots aber nicht, laedt die Recovery einen V1-Snapshot und wendet V2-Events darauf an - falsche Form, still kaputter State. Entweder beide oder keiner."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_onrecoverycomplete_always_fires", "label": "onRecoveryComplete feuert auch ohne Events", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Einmal, nachdem der initiale State eingerichtet ist. Die Falle ist wann: nach preStart, vor dem ersten Command - die Mailbox-Verarbeitung wird erst nach der Rueckkehr wieder aufgenommen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_choosing_the_snapshot_interval", "label": "Das Snapshot-Intervall waehlen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drei Zahlen zaehlen: Recovery-Zeit (niedrigeres N ist schneller), Schreibkosten (jeder Snapshot serialisiert den vollstaendigen State, hoeheres N amortisiert) und Storage. Nicht uebertunen."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_everynevents", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_recovery_flow_with_snapshots", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_recovery_flow_with_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore_catalog", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_retention_best_effort_write_is_not", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore_catalog", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotadapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_adapter_pairing_rule", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_onrecoverycomplete_always_fires", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_recovery_flow_with_snapshots", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_choosing_the_snapshot_interval", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_everynevents", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshot_stores_in_memory_inmemorysnapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_snapshot_stores_sqlite_sqlitesnapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_f